From 39fe58d876e0ee3f0abcbe5d65bb935acb26c443 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:52:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D7: a partial transaction edit keeps the fields it does not
 send

POST /transaction/:id read an absent memo as "emptied" and an absent
`cleared` as "unticked", so an API caller that only moved a date wiped the
memo and marked the entry uncleared under "Saved."; an absent amount was
refused outright. A browser sends nothing for an unticked checkbox, so the
route could not tell "unticked" from "not mentioned".

The edit form now sends a `cleared_present` marker beside the checkbox, as
it already did for `reimbursable`. A flag is set from its own field when
sent, unset when only its marker is sent, and kept otherwise. An absent memo
or amount keeps the stored value; the form always sends both, so emptying
the memo box still clears it and a blank amount is still refused. Tags,
owner, payee, direction, date and envelope lines already kept their values
when absent. docs/API.md now states the partial-edit semantics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zXWwzys3K4XksLh3rrcKu
